    "biography": {
      "concept": "Prints the Stillwater Sentinel and hands it out on the corner (Act 2)",
      "notes": "Amos Teague prints the Stillwater Sentinel and hands it out on the corner with ink to the elbows. Today's edition: HALLOWEEN PARADE TODAY, BAND TO PLAY 'SAINTS', FLOATS AT 3, TRAIN AT 4:10. The ink is always wet; he's never needed a second edition. He is cheerful, proud and inky, a small-town newspaperman who loves a headline. He wears a fedora with a PRESS card in the band, which is not a costume, which is the joke."
    }
